{title: Your Good Pleasure}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
1. You came into my heart,
And You made my life complete.
All that I called my own,
I lay before Your feet.

Verse 2
Seeking Your honor,
Now and forever,
Guide me each step of the way...

Verse 3
C. Please be in me,
Work deep in me,
To will and to do,
To will and to do,
To will and to do Your good pleasure.

Verse 4
2. Called by Your Spirit, Lord,
To follow where You lead.
To trust You every hour
To meet my every need.

Verse 5
Speak to my heart, Lord,
For I will answer;
May I be true to Your call...

Verse 6
C. Please be in me,
Work deep in me,
To will and to do,
To will and to do,
To will and to do Your good pleasure.
